#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hearth's AI hub (shell/services/Ai.qml, README "AI").

One place for every model the desktop uses: local servers (Ollama,
llama.cpp's llama-server in router mode) and coding-agent CLIs (Claude
Code, Codex, Gemini). It lists installed and loaded models, loads and
unloads them, pulls new ones, reports VRAM per GPU and per process, and
runs the assistant (voice and Spotlight's "Ask") with tools.

JSON lines on stdin/stdout, so the shell never waits:

  {"cmd": "refresh"}                      -> {"type": "state", ...}
  {"cmd": "watch", "on": true}            poll every 2 s while a UI shows it
  {"cmd": "load"|"unload", "provider": "ollama", "model": "qwen3.5:4b"}
  {"cmd": "unloadAll"}
  {"cmd": "pull", "provider": "ollama", "model": "..."}   -> {"type": "pull", ...}
  {"cmd": "delete", "provider": "ollama", "model": "..."}
  {"cmd": "server", "provider": "llamacpp", "on": true}   (systemd user unit)
  {"cmd": "ask", "id": 3, "feature": "assistant", "text": "...", "context": {...}}
      -> {"type": "tool", "id": 3, "call": 1, "name": "launch_app", "args": {...}}
         (the shell runs it and answers {"cmd": "toolResult", "id": 3, "call": 1, "result": "..."})
      -> {"type": "reply", "id": 3, "text": "...", "done": true}
  {"cmd": "cancel", "id": 3}

Settings come from settings.json `ai` (Settings > AI). Cloud CLIs are used
only when `ai.allowCloud` is on.
"""

